---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- BOSS DISCOVERY UNDER STREAMING (v1550)
--
-- Bosses we do not spawn ourselves (Tairock, Chakra Knight, Hyuga, Shukaku,
-- Matatabi, Isobu, Haku, Wooden Golem, Gaara) just exist in the world, and
-- the farm finds them with workspace:FindFirstChild(workspaceName). Since
-- v1550 turned StreamingEnabled on, a boss we are not standing near is not
-- replicated to this client at all, so that lookup always fails.
--
-- Ask the engine for the arena instead of walking there. This does not move
-- the character, which is why it beats a probe-teleport: no position jump, no
-- landing in unloaded space, and no showing up in the arena while Safe TP is
-- trying to keep us unseen.
--
-- Anchor priority: an explicit streamPos, else the reward position (always
-- inside the arena), else the spawn position.
---------------------------------------------------------------------
---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Event-variant boss names
--
-- The game reskins bosses for seasonal events and the variant REPLACES the
-- base NPC in workspace, so a farm that only knows the base name finds
-- nothing for the whole event. `alternateName` carries those variants.
--
-- It is a LIST because a boss can have one per event, and because the names
-- are not consistently formed - there is no rule to derive them from, so each
-- is listed explicitly (all verified against the GameManager NPC configs):
--
--   Tairock           -> "Enchanted Tairock"      (prefix)
--   Barbarit The Rose -> "Barbarit The Hallowed"  (infix)
--   Barbarit The Rose -> "Frosted The Rose"       (drops "Barbarit" entirely!)
--   Lavarossa         -> "Hallowed Lavarossa"     (prefix)
--
-- A plain string is still accepted, so an entry that was never converted
-- keeps working.
--
-- >>> WHEN A NEW EVENT SHIPS, ADD ITS VARIANT NAMES HERE. Do not hand-   <<<
-- >>> check them; run, against a fresh GameManager dump:                 <<<
-- >>>   python -I tools/find_boss_variants.py "Bloodlines/Game Scripts"  <<<
-- >>> It prints paste-ready alternateName lists. It matches variants to   <<<
-- >>> a base boss by CONFIG FINGERPRINT (Idle, RequiredSounds,            <<<
-- >>> AcumenReward, attack names) rather than by name, which is the only  <<<
-- >>> way "Frosted The Rose" gets found - it shares no token with         <<<
-- >>> "Barbarit The Rose" but has a byte-identical fingerprint.          <<<
---------------------------------------------------------------------
function _0xa299._0xAltNames(config)
    local alt = config and config.alternateName
    if not alt then return {} end
    if type(alt) == "string" then return { alt } end
    return alt
end

-- Is this boss replicated to us right now, under any name the search accepts?
function _0xa299._0xBossPresent(config)
    if not config then return nil end
    local names = { config.workspaceName, "Farming " .. config.workspaceName }
    for _, alt in ipairs(_0xa299._0xAltNames(config)) do
        table.insert(names, alt)
        table.insert(names, "Farming " .. alt)
    end
    for _, n in ipairs(names) do
        local m = workspace:FindFirstChild(n)
        if m then return m end
    end
    return nil
end

-- ONE-SHOT DISCOVERY SWEEP.
--
-- Earlier this trickled two arena requests per second, which was the bug: the
-- finder ran through all the selected bosses and concluded "none spawned" long
-- before most arenas had even been requested, so bosses that were alive the
-- whole time were treated as absent and skipped.
--
-- Measured live: a request costs 0.05-0.18 s and sweeping NINE arenas took
-- 0.97 s total - and turned 3 visible bosses into 7 (Hyuga, Isobu, Haku,
-- Gaara and Tairock were all alive but not replicated). So sweep everything
-- selected up front and only then decide what is spawned. Throttled, since a
-- boss that is genuinely dead stays dead for a while.
_0xa299._0xSweepAt = 0

---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- GO AND LOOK  (the sweep is not enough on its own)
--
-- RequestStreamAroundAsync is RANGE LIMITED. Measured 2026-10-22 from 2721
-- (Shukaku), 2981 (Matatabi) and 3241 (Isobu) studs: every call returned "ok"
-- in 186-242 ms having delivered essentially NOTHING - 0 to 1 parts within 300
-- studs of the arena anchor and no ground under it, against 2382 parts within
-- 300 studs of the player at the same moment. The one part that did arrive was
-- a Locations marker, not arena geometry.
--
-- So the up-front sweep only helps for arenas we are already near. Streaming
-- follows the player's REAL position, which means the only thing that brings a
-- cross-map boss in is going there. That is what this does: when a boss we do
-- not spawn ourselves cannot be found, travel to its arena with _0xSTP (which
-- pre-streams and holds position until the floor exists) and look again before
-- concluding it is not in the server.
--
-- This is what made the old Tailed Beast Farm report beasts as missing when
-- they were in the server all along - the beast arenas are in far corners of
-- the map, so they were never once within sweep range.
--
-- Only fires when the boss is ALREADY not found, so it cannot change anything
-- for a boss that the sweep or plain proximity already resolved.
---------------------------------------------------------------------
_0xa299._0xArenaRevisit = 20   -- seconds before walking to the same arena again

-- Bosses the farm spawns itself by firing an activate event. THE one list -
-- every check below reads it, because this was previously spelled out as an
-- "or" chain in three separate places plus an array, and re-enabling Lava
-- Snake and The Ringed Samurai updated the array but not the chains, so those
-- two were never actually reaching the spawn branch.
--
-- These do not need the streaming sweep or the travel fallback: an unspawned
-- boss does not exist anywhere, so pulling its arena in cannot reveal it. The
-- farm goes to spawnPosition and fires the event instead.
_0xa299._0xSpawnableBosses = {
    ["Lava Rosa"] = true,
    ["Manda"] = true,
    ["Barbarit The Rose"] = true,
    ["Lava Snake"] = true,
    ["The Ringed Samurai"] = true,
}

