    S.bossMissingSince = nil
    return nil, false
end

--[[ DISABLED 2026-10-25 at the user's request: the Gaara work is unfinished and needs another pass, so it is parked rather than shipped half-done. Re-enable by removing this block comment and the matching ones at the boss config entry, the customDanger call site and the four toggles, and by putting "Gaara" back in _0xa299._0xc152 and _bossList.
---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- GAARA - world-state dodges (rewritten after watching a live fight)
--
-- The first version guessed at where these things live and was wrong on both
-- counts, which is why it "barely worked":
--
--   * The pyramid hitbox is **`SandMasoleumHitbox`, a MeshPart parented
--     straight to `workspace`** - not nil-parented, and not a Folder under
--     workspace.Debris. So neither the Debris folder scan NOR the
--     getnilinstances() scan could ever match it. Observed spawning TWICE per
--     cast, 5-30 studs from the boss, ~2.5 s each.
--   * The sandstorm is NOT `workspace.Debris.Sandstorm.Storm`;
--     `Debris:FindFirstChild("Sandstorm")` was verified nil. There is a
--     `workspace.Sandstorms` folder, but its 4 entries are ambient MAP
--     sandstorms 3500-5100 studs from the arena - nothing to do with Gaara.
--     Gaara's own storm shows up as a `Sandstorm` Model in workspace.Debris,
--     so match on the NAME and require it to be near the boss.
--
-- It was also far too expensive to run per frame:
--     getnilinstances()  = 75 ms for 35,366 instances   (was called 20x/sec)
--     Debris child scan  = 2.2 ms for 5,030 children    (was called per frame)
--     targeted FindFirstChild = 0.002 ms
-- So this is now EVENT-DRIVEN: ChildAdded/ChildRemoved on workspace and
-- workspace.Debris maintain a tiny bit of state, and the per-frame call is
-- just a couple of comparisons. No scanning at all.
--
-- Other Gaara effects seen near the boss, if more dodges are ever wanted:
--   Sand Suspension Mastered (Model, Debris, ~91-157 studs, has Hitbox/Cloud)
--   Big Sand Slash (Part, Debris, 0 studs)
--   Sand ShieldGaara / SandShieldEmit / SandShieldEnd (Model+Parts, 4 studs)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- STAGE 2
--
-- Gaara has four stages. They are plain boolean attributes on the boss model
-- (GameManager 7809-7831), so the stage is readable at any time:
--     workspace.Gaara:GetAttribute("Stage2")
-- Stage 2 starts at Stage2Percentage = 95, i.e. after only 5% of his 1500 HP,
-- so in practice the whole fight after the opening is stage 2 or later.
--
-- Stage 2 is not just "stage 1 but faster". Three moves are gated to it
-- (Stages = { "Stage2" } in the boss config ~57640-57692), and none of them
-- existed while the stage-1 dodges were being written:
--
--   Sand Shield      dmg 25 x 20 reps @ 0.25s, StunTime 2, RAGDOLLS, radius 30
--   Sand Coffin      dmg 50, StunTime 2.1, homing projectile
--   Sand Suspension  dmg 30, CD 300 (once a fight)
--
-- Every one of them is `Blockable = false`, so blocking cannot save us the way
-- it does against the Wooden Golem's pillars - the only counter is to not be
-- in the volume. All three are therefore dodged by HEIGHT, which is what the
-- rest of this handler already does.
--
-- SAND SHIELD is the one that actually kills a hovering farm:
--   * `require(ServerStorage.SkillManager):sandShield(...)` parents the shield
--     into workspace.Debris as `"Sand Shield" .. boss.Name`, i.e.
--     "Sand ShieldGaara". That ChildAdded fires at the START of the move,
--     before the first damage tick - the earliest signal the client gets.
--   * The launch then does `v430.SpatialQueryRadius = 30` (GameManager 8708),
--     OVERRIDING the 16 in the boss config. The real danger sphere is 30
--     studs around the boss, and the farm hovers at offset 10 - squarely
--     inside it.
--   * Each tick (GameManager 8137-8166) fires `sandShieldSpikes` to everyone
--     within 500, knocks the victim with CreateVelocity 80, and then calls
--     `t4:RagdollCharacter(Parent, true, StunTime)`. That is the ragdoll.
--   * It runs `task.wait(5)` before stopping, so the height has to be held
--     for the whole 5 s, not just a moment.
--
-- SAND COFFIN is much less dangerous to a hovering farm than its damage
-- suggests, and the reason is worth recording so nobody "fixes" it later.
-- Its steering loop (GameManager 8765-8775) is:
--     local v507 = Vector3.new(Position.X, Position2.Y, Position.Z)
--     local v508 = v507 - Position2
--     DirectionalBV.Velocity = v508.Unit * 70
-- `v507` takes the projectile's OWN Y, so v508.Y is exactly 0 and the
-- BodyVelocity is purely horizontal. It re-aims at us every frame at 70
-- studs/s but can never climb. Its Hitbox is 10x8x10 scaled 1.5 -> 15x12x15,
-- centred 3 studs under the boss's HumanoidRootPart, so the top of the hitbox
-- is only bossY + 3. A small lift clears it permanently.
---------------------------------------------------------------------
_0xa299._0xGaaraNear = 200    -- studs from the boss; ignores map-wide copies
-- Pyramid: 30 -> 47 -> 50. The original 30 only just held it, and also sat
-- exactly ON the Sand Shield's 30-stud boundary. Losing melee range during a
-- dodge does not matter - not being hit is worth more than the uptime.
_0xa299._0xGaaraPyramidOffset = 50
-- Storm: 25 -> 40. 25 was never confirmed to actually hold; the storm is a
-- Model whose cloud has real vertical extent, so give it clearance.
_0xa299._0xGaaraStormOffset = 40
-- SpatialQueryRadius is forced to 30 at cast time; clear it with margin.
_0xa299._0xGaaraShieldOffset = 38
-- The coffin was first given 16, reasoned from its hitbox geometry: 10x8x10
-- scaled 1.5 is 15x12x15 centred at bossY-3, so the top should be bossY+3.
-- A live fight disproved that. Logged twice, from a farm hovering at offset
-- 10, the coffin spawned at dY=-13 (exactly bossY-3) and landed its hit
-- anyway, identified positively by the knockback power: the coffin's crush
-- fires `CreateVelocity ... 40` (GameManager 8247) and the log shows
-- "KNOCKBACK power 40" + 40 damage ~3 s after each spawn. So its real
-- vertical reach is at least 13 studs above its own centre, not 6, and the
-- hit is evidently not the Hitbox part's bounds alone.
--
-- Rather than guess a replacement from geometry that has already been wrong
-- once, the coffin now uses the SAME height as the shield. 38 clears the
-- observed reach by ~25 studs, and both moves are short windows, so there is
-- nothing to gain from a tighter number.
_0xa299._0xGaaraCoffinOffset = 38

-- SAND STORM: hold block through it instead of flying out.
--
-- See the storm branch in _0xGaaraDodge for why this works (the move is
-- Blockable, and BreakBlockLight only breaks a block on a hit to the BACK).
-- Set false to go back to leaving on _0xGaaraStormOffset.
_0xa299._0xGaaraStormBlock = true
-- Grace on the blocking state. One storm tick is 0.5 s and the whole move is
-- 8 of them, so this is long enough to bridge a frame where the instance
-- blinks but short enough that we are back on him promptly once it ends.
_0xa299._0xGaaraStormBlockHold = 0.6
-- The shield's own `task.wait(5)`, plus a moment for the last tick to pass.
_0xa299._0xGaaraShieldHold = 5.5
-- The coffin is destroyed by Debris:AddItem(clone, 4) and anchored at 4 s.
_0xa299._0xGaaraCoffinHold = 4.5
-- Sand Suspension: the ring spawns the attack at ground + 3.6 with
-- Duration = 10, but it is a ground effect, so the storm height clears it.
_0xa299._0xGaaraSuspOffset = 30
_0xa299._0xGaaraSuspHold = 3

-- COFFIN / SUSPENSION: answer them by teleporting to the four far spots
-- instead of climbing to an offset.
--
-- Both are good candidates for it. The coffin is a homing projectile that
-- re-aims every frame and whose real vertical reach turned out to be larger
-- than its hitbox suggested (see _0xGaaraCoffinOffset), and suspension is a
-- ground effect we only learn about from a remote with no instance to track.
-- Leaving the area outright sidesteps both problems, where an offset is a bet
-- on a number.
--
-- Costs nothing extra in damage: at the 38/30 offsets we are already out of
-- melee reach, so neither path lands hits during the window.
_0xa299._0xGaaraCoffinSuspRoam = false
-- Grace on the teleport-dodge window, refreshed each frame the move is live.
-- Must exceed one hop (_0xGaaraV2Step, 0.3 s) or the cycle would end between
-- hops while the move was still up.
_0xa299._0xGaaraTeleDodgeHold = 0.5

_0xa299._0xGaaraRoamEvery = 10    -- seconds between hops
_0xa299._0xGaaraRoamHold  = 1     -- seconds spent at the spot
_0xa299._0xGaaraStormClear = 10   -- keep this far from any sandstorm
-- How long a ring's area stays off-limits after its warning. The warning
-- itself is only 0.5 s, but the Sand Suspension it precedes runs with
-- Duration = 10, so the ground stays dangerous well after the ring appears.
_0xa299._0xGaaraRingAvoid = 12
-- Smallest radius to assume for a ground indicator when its own Size reads
-- tiny, which happens because createCrack spawns at (0.1, 1, 1) and grows
-- into the real disc over 0.25 s.
_0xa299._0xGaaraIndicatorMin = 12
-- How long a spot stays blacklisted after we were damaged standing on it.
_0xa299._0xGaaraHurtAvoid = 15

_0xa299._0xGaaraRoam = { nextAt = 0, doneAt = 0, target = nil, spot = nil, hpAtSpot = nil }

_0xa299._0xGaaraState = {
    armed = false,
    conns = {},
    pyramid = nil,        -- the live SandMasoleumHitbox, if any
    pyramidUntil = 0,     -- hold the height until this time (gone + 1 s)
    storm = nil,          -- the live Sandstorm model, if any
    shield = nil,         -- the live "Sand Shield<boss>" model, if any
    shieldUntil = 0,      -- hold the height for the move's full 5 s
    coffin = nil,         -- the live "Sand Coffin<boss>" projectile, if any
    coffinUntil = 0,
    suspUntil = 0,        -- set by the circleWarning remote; no instance to hold
    -- Refreshed by the dodge every frame a storm is up and we are choosing to
    -- block it rather than leave. A deadline rather than a boolean so the
    -- state survives a frame where the storm instance blinks, and so it clears
    -- itself if the dodge stops running at all (farm off, boss switched).
    stormBlockUntil = 0,
    -- Same idea for the moves we answer by teleporting to the far spots
    -- instead of climbing (coffin, suspension). Refreshed every frame their
    -- window is live; see _0xGaaraCoffinSuspRoam.
    teleDodgeUntil = 0,
    animBoss = nil,       -- boss model whose Animator we hooked
    animConn = nil,
    -- Every live sandstorm, not just the most recent one. The single `storm`
    -- above is enough to decide a hover height, but the roam has to check a
    -- candidate spot against ALL of them.
    storms = {},
    -- Live red rings from circleWarning: { pos, radius, expires }.
    rings = {},
    -- Live ground-indicator INSTANCES (the red circle). Kept as instances, not
    -- positions, so the radius is read off real geometry each time.
    indicators = {},
    -- Spots we were damaged on: { pos, expires }. The name-independent
    -- backstop for an indicator we cannot identify.
    hurtSpots = {},
