local GAARA_PYRAMID = { ["SandMasoleumHitbox"] = true }
local GAARA_STORM   = { ["Sandstorm"] = true }

-- GROUND INDICATORS (the red circle)
--
-- The ring the player SEES is a replicated instance, not the circleWarning
-- remote. That remote has no handler anywhere in the decompiled client, which
-- was noted early and then not acted on - the roam's ring avoidance was built
-- on circleWarning alone, so an indicator appearing on an occupied spot was
-- ignored exactly as reported.
--
-- `crack` is the one confirmed from source: GameManager.createCrack /
-- spawnCrack clone ServerStorage.Models.crack, set the CFrame BEFORE
-- parenting to workspace.Debris, and tween the Size to
-- Vector3.new(0.3, Radius, Radius) - i.e. a flat disc of that radius, which
-- is what a ground indicator looks like.
--
-- `NORMAL_SAND_RING` is from a live log: it appeared in Debris 32 studs from
-- Gaara and vanished again. Its mesh lives in an Effects module so there is
-- no source to read, hence matching by name.
--
-- Plain `SandRing` is deliberately NOT here. The same log had it spawning in
-- large numbers (dozens at a time, mostly from other players' effects), so it
-- reads as storm decoration; treating each as a hazard would mark most of the
-- arena unsafe and stop the roam entirely. Sandstorms are already avoided by
-- _0xGaaraStormClear.
--
-- Radius is taken from the part's LIVE Size rather than assumed, which also
-- handles createCrack's 0.25 s grow-in without needing to know the tween.
local GAARA_INDICATOR = {
    ["crack"] = true,
    ["NORMAL_SAND_RING"] = true,
